1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:07,003
BridgeBack helps people understand housing paperwork and prepare their next useful step.

2
00:00:07,003 --> 00:00:16,003
Fictional practice: two forms are waiting for income proof. Checklist progress is
calculated from state.

3
00:00:16,003 --> 00:00:26,007
The dependency graph connects shared documents to separate program requirements. OR means
one accepted option.

4
00:00:26,007 --> 00:00:38,013
Preview one action with the same engine. The hypothetical result leaves saved progress
untouched.

5
00:00:38,013 --> 00:00:48,022
Apply the document only when it is actually available. The two fictional forms can now
proceed.

6
00:00:48,022 --> 00:01:00,025
Cannot get the pay stub? Route Rescue checks the exact alternatives instead of inventing
an exception.

7
00:01:00,025 --> 00:01:12,033
A stuck step gets smaller instructions. Reviewing help or requesting a paper does not mark
it ready.

8
00:01:12,033 --> 00:01:20,038
A short fictional exercise explains gross pay. Learning answers do not change personal
income or readiness.

9
00:01:20,038 --> 00:01:34,043
Real public counselor listings are separate from the sample rules. Source date, languages
and search area are visible.

10
00:01:34,043 --> 00:01:44,050
Prepare focused questions and record that you are waiting. No call, application or
document completion is fabricated.

11
00:01:44,050 --> 00:01:53,058
No account or document uploads. People control exports and deletion; browser storage is
not encrypted secure storage.

12
00:01:53,058 --> 00:02:00,062
TypeScript, Next.js/React, IndexedDB and Capacitor/Swift. Review footage: add entrant
names, your own narration and full AI disclosure.
